CLOVEROS - start the CloverOS desktop
Usage: cloveros [--help] [--version] [--apps]

Leaves the text shell and starts the CloverOS GNOME-style desktop for the
current user. The session is the same one the graphical login screen starts,
so anything you can do there you can do from here.

Options:
  --help, -h   show this help and exit
  --version, -v  print the CloverOS version and exit
  --apps      list the applications available to the desktop and exit

Examples:
  cloveros            start the desktop
  cloveros --apps     show what is installed
  cloveros --version  print the version

Desktop keys:
  F1..F4      terminal, files, settings, system information
  F5          Activities overview (application grid and window switcher)
  F6 / F7     snap the focused window left or right
  F8          maximise or restore the focused window
  F10         log out and return to this shell
  alt+tab     cycle between open windows
  ctrl+alt+t  open a terminal window
  escape      close a menu or the overview

Notes:
- The command cannot run when the shell is captured, piped or backgrounded;
  a desktop needs the whole terminal.
- Logging out with F10 ends the session and logs you out of CloverOS, because
  the desktop took over the shell you started it from.
- If the desktop files are not installed, the command says so and leaves you
  in the text shell; run the installer again to add them.
